Imports:
  - Types:
      - ExcalidrawElement
    From: packages/element/src

Usages:
  host_app_state: |
    perform/label/icon/keyTest callbacks receive the host application's current element
    list and app state (current tool, selection, viewport, style defaults) as plain parameters.
    This cell treats that shape opaquely rather than formally importing a concrete type from the
    root packages/excalidraw cell, to avoid a dependency cycle (the root cell composes this
    one). See packages/element/src's own `host_app_state` usage for the identical pattern.

Annotations: |
  This is Excalidraw's action-registry extension point: the mechanism for adding a new
  user-triggerable operation (menu item, keyboard shortcut, context-menu entry, or
  programmatic-API call) without modifying any dispatch code elsewhere. An action is a plain
  object conforming to the `Action` contract, appended to a shared module-level list via
  `register`; every UI surface (menus, shortcuts, the imperative API) reads from that same list,
  so a correctly-registered action is automatically available everywhere without further wiring.

  Use `host_app_state` for how perform/label/icon/keyTest receive application state. perform
  receives the current scene's elements as `ExcalidrawElement` (from Imports) instances.

---

"Action(name: string, label: string, perform: Function)":
  location: types.ts
  annotations: |
    The contract every action implements. perform is the only required behavior; everything
    else customizes how the action surfaces in menus/shortcuts/the command palette.
  properties:
    "name -> string": |
      Stable identifier, drawn from a fixed closed set of known action names.
    "label -> string": |
      Display text (or a function of current elements/appState/app producing display text) shown
      in menus and the command palette.
    "keywords -> Array<string> | undefined": |
      Extra search terms so the command palette can find this action by synonyms.
    "keyTest -> Function | undefined": |
      Optional predicate over a keyboard event deciding whether this action's shortcut matched.
    "predicate -> Function | undefined": |
      Optional predicate deciding whether the action should currently be offered at all (e.g.
      hidden when nothing is selected).
  methods:
    "perform(elements: Array<ExcalidrawElement>, appState: any, formData: any, app: any) -> result:any": |
      Execute the action. Returns a result shape carrying the elements/appState to apply and a
      capture-update directive controlling undo/redo history recording (see
      packages/element/src's Store cell for how increments are captured).

      `elements`, `appState`: see `host_app_state`

      Constraints:
      - Must be a pure function of its arguments plus whatever the action itself owns — must not
        reach into module-level or global mutable state to decide its result

"register(action: Action) -> action:Action":
  location: register.ts
  annotations: |
    The extension point's entry point: appends `action` to the shared, module-level action list
    read by every UI surface (menus, keyboard shortcuts, command palette, the imperative API).
    Returns the same action back (for convenient `export const fooAction = register({...})`
    call-site style).

    `action`: an object conforming to `Action`
    Returns: the same `action`, unchanged

    Constraints:
    - This is the ONLY sanctioned way to make a new operation available across the app; adding a
      parallel dispatch path (e.g. a bespoke keydown listener or a menu item wired directly to a
      handler function, bypassing this list) duplicates the mechanism instead of extending it.

"ActionManager(app: any)":
  location: manager.tsx
  annotations: |
    Runtime consumer of the registered action list: looks up an action by name or matches a
    keyboard event against every registered action's keyTest, then executes it and applies its
    result to the scene/app state.

    `app`: see `host_app_state`
  methods:
    "registerAction(action: Action)": |
      Add one action to this manager's lookup table (by name); used for actions supplied by a
      host integration rather than the built-in registry.
    "executeAction(action: Action, source: string, value: any) -> result:any": |
      Run action.perform with the current elements/appState/app, guarding against execution
      while the editor is non-interactive (except for source: "api" programmatic calls), then
      apply the returned result to the scene.

      `source`: which UI surface triggered this ("ui" | "keyboard" | "contextMenu" | "api" |
      "commandPalette")

